title: 'Staking: Chill stakers should not have a score'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Port of #9926 from `pallet-staking-async` to `pallet-staking`: `ScoreProvider::score` now
    returns `None` for a bonded stash that is neither a nominator nor a validator.

    Previously any bonded stash had a score. Recent versions of `pallet-bags-list` insert any
    account they are asked to rebag that is missing from the list but has a score, so a chilled
    staker could be put back into `VoterList`:

    - by anyone, through the permissionless `rebag` call, and
    - by the `on_idle` auto-rebag, if the staker chilled while the auto-rebag cursor
      (`NextNodeAutoRebagged`) pointed at them. The cursor is processed first even if it has left
      the list in the meantime.

    Such a node is neither a nominator nor a validator, so every election snapshot hits the
    "invalid item in `VoterList`" defensive failure, and it takes up a spot in the voter list. This
    was observed on Versi after validators chilled to shrink the validator set. With this change,
    existing stale nodes have no score, so the next `rebag` or auto-rebag of them removes them.
crates:
- name: pallet-staking
  bump: patch
